8. Bb5+ { This move isn't as common as the other two, but it's worth knowing what to do against it. White wants to disrupt Black's plan of attacking the d4-pawn. } 8... Nc6 { Black calmly blocks the check. A few fireworks can go off in this position, but there is no danger for either side. } 9. O-O { White castles and brings the king to safety. } (9. d5 { seems to win a piece. However, after } 9... Qa5 10. Rb1 a6 11. Bxc6+ bxc6 12. O-O O-O 13. dxc6 Bg4 { Black will eventually win the pawn back and achieve an even game. }) 9... O-O { This move has recently become much more popular than the alternative ...cxd4. Black gets the king to safety and prepares to launch an all-out attack against the pawn on d4. } 10. Be3 { White shores up the defense of the d4-pawn and develops their last minor piece. } (10. Bxc6 bxc6 11. Qc2 cxd4 12. cxd4 Bg4 { has also been played, but after } 13. Ne5 Qxd4 14. Bb2 Qb6 15. Rab1 Bxe5 16. Bxe5 Qa5 { the position is even. }) 10... Bg4 { This move pins the f3-knight, removing a key defender of d4. } 11. d5 { White advances the pawn because defending it was becoming too difficult. } (11. Bxc6 bxc6 12. Rc1 Qa5 { has also been played here. The position is even. }) (11. dxc5 Bxc3 12. Rc1 Bg7 { poses no problems at all for Black. }) 11... Ne5 { Black centralizes the knight and puts a lot of pressure on the pinned knight on f3. } 12. Be2 { White has to move the bishop back to protect the f3-knight. } 12... Nxf3+ { Black exchanges, knowing that the resulting position will be good for them. } 13. Bxf3 { Recapturing. } (13. gxf3 Bh3 { would be horrible. }) 13... Bxf3 { Black continues to exchange. } 14. Qxf3 { White recaptures. } 14... Bxc3 { Black takes the c3-pawn and attacks White's rook on a1. } 15. Rab1 { Sidestepping the threat and going after the pawn on b7. } 15... b6 { Protecting the b7-pawn. } 16. Bxc5 { This tactic wins White's pawn back. } 16... Rc8 { Bringing the rook to the open c-file. Black has achieved equality. } (16... bxc5 17. Qxc3 { would leave Black with a poor pawn structure and a huge target on c5. While this isn't too bad, there's no reason to opt for this. }) *


