4. Nf3 { This is the Three Knights Variation of the Grunfeld. White doesn't try to immediately go for a strong pawn center and focuses on development instead. In the Three Knights Variation, White maintains quite a bit of flexibility. } 4... Bg7 { Black completes the fianchetto and prepares to castle Kingside. Now White has a large host of options. We will examine White's four main moves: Qb3, Bg5, e3, and Bf4.
5. cxd5 is also possible, transposing into the 7. Nf3 line of the Exchange Variation. } *


