8. Nf3 { This move was favored by Petrosian and Seirawan. White simply retreats the knight, knowing that Black's g7-bishop will bite on granite after e2-e3. } 8... exd5 { Black restores the material balance. } 9. e3 (9. b4 { was Seirawan's pet variation. He had excellent success with the move, but more recently Black has found satisfactory ways to deal with this. } 9... Qd6 10. a3 (10. Qb3 Nc6 11. e3 Qxb4 12. Qxb4 Nxb4 { is good for Black. }) 10... O-O 11. e3 c6 12. Be2 a5 { is slightly better for Black. }) 9... a5 { This move, restraining White's minority attack, has been very successful for Black. Black scores 63% in this variation! } 10. Be2 { Developing the bishop and preparing to castle. } (10. Bd3 O-O 11. O-O c6 12. a3 Re8 { has also been tried. Black is doing well. }) 10... O-O { Black brings the King to safety. } 11. O-O { White does the same. } 11... Re8 { Black brings the rook to the semi-open e-file. } 12. a3 { White prepares b2-b4, launching a minority attack. } 12... Bf8 { Black doesn't allow this to happen! Black is doing well in this position. } *


