[Orientation "black"]

6. Bf4 { Just like the 6. Bh4 variation, White keeps the bishop pair. } 6... Nxc3 { Black exchanges knights, similar to the previous variation. } 7. bxc3 { White recaptures. } 7... c5 { Black strikes in the center. } (7... dxc4 { has also been played, with good results. }) (7... O-O { is a third option, albeit less popular than the other two. }) 8. e3 { White defends the d4 and c4-pawns and prepares to develop the bishop on f1. } (8. cxd5 cxd4 9. cxd4 Qxd5 10. e3 Nc6 11. Be2 O-O { transposes to the main line. }) 8... O-O { Black gets the King to safety. } 9. cxd5 { White doesn't want to be forced to move the bishop twice by recapturing on c4, so pawns are exchanged. White can now develop the bishop more easily. } 9... cxd4 { Black throws in this exchange before recapturing on d5. } (9... Qxd5 { is also fine here, I just prefer to play ...cxd4 first. }) 10. cxd4 { White captures toward the center. } 10... Qxd5 { Black gets the d5-pawn back. The pawn structure is similar to that of an Exchange Variation, with White having a central majority and Black having a queenside majority. However, White's majority is less dangerous because they have not managed to push their pawn to e4. } 11. Be2 { White prepares to castle. } 11... Nc6 { Black develops the knight. } 12. O-O { White gets the King to safety. } 12... Bf5 { Developing the bishop to an active diagonal and connecting rooks. This move also controls the important e4-square. } 13. Qa4 { White brings the queen out and connects rooks. } 13... Qa5 { Black offers an exchange of queens, knowing that the queenside majority will give good play in the endgame. } 14. Qxa5 { White accepts the queen trade. } (14. Qb3 { declines the offer. Black insists on the trade with } 14... Qb4 15. Rfc1 Qxb3 16. axb3 Rfd8 { , achieving a decent position. }) 14... Nxa5 { Black recaptures. } 15. Rfc1 { Bringing the rook to the open c-file. } (15. Nd2 Rac8 16. Rfc1 Be6 { has also been played. Black is fine here. }) 15... Rfc8 { Black challenges for control of the file. } 16. Nd2 { White reroutes the knight to greener pastures on the queenside. } 16... Rxc1+ { Black exchanges rooks. } 17. Rxc1 { White recaptures. } 17... Rc8 { Black offers to exchange the other pair of rooks. } 18. Rxc8+ { White obliges, reaching a minor piece endgame. } 18... Bxc8 { Recapturing the rook. The position is fine for Black. } *


