[UTCTime "12:39:23"]
[Orientation "black"]

7. Ne5 { This move leads to some pretty interesting games. } 7... O-O { White now has the option to transpose to 7. Nc3 lines or to keep options open. } 8. Nc3 (8. O-O { is quite flexible. } 8... Ne4 9. Nd2 (9. Nc3 Nxc3 10. bxc3 Nc6 11. Nxc6 bxc6 12. Qa4 Qb6 13. Ba3 Qa6 14. Qxa6 Bxa6 { is fine for Black. }) (9. f3 Nd6 10. Nc3 e6 11. e4 dxe4 12. fxe4 Nc6 { is also critical, but Black is fine here. }) 9... Nxd2 10. Bxd2 Nd7 11. Bc3 Nf6 { is okay for Black. }) 8... b6 { leads us back to the 7.Nc3 chapter as seen above. } *


