[Orientation "black"]

5. Nf3 dxc4 { Not the most usual, but this move is a nice way to avoid White's usual system in this opening. It also gives Black a fine position. } 6. O-O Bg7 7. a4 (7. Ne5 Ng4 { counters the knight advancement very well. } 8. f4 Nxe5 9. fxe5 O-O { is better for Black. }) 7... Ne4 { Heading for d6 to defend the pawn on c4. } 8. Qc2 (8. Nc3 Nd6 9. e4 Bg4 10. Be3 Qc8 { is fine for Black. }) 8... Nd6 9. e4 Na6 { Eyeing b4. } 10. Na3 O-O { Black doesn't have many weaknesses and should be fine. } *


